 fields), and smoothing rates (molt_stress_rise/decay_smoothing) — instead of hardcoded 0.5/0.3/0.2, 0.3/0.3/0.2/0.2/0.3, and 0.2/0.05","fr-7-96901ca8 VERIFIED FIXED: compute_mortality_probabilities at shrimp.rs:1200-1201 now uses params.molt_stress_mortality_threshold instead of hardcoded 0.5; field defined at biology.rs:335 with default 0.5","fr-7-b39b6c90 VERIFIED FIXED: molt_mineral_modifier at shrimp.rs:1678-1702 now uses params.molt_gh_excess_penalty_divisor (default 10.0) and params.molt_mineral_factor_floor (default 0.3) with defensive guards (.max(0.01) and .clamp(0.0,1.0))","fr-7-1cbde9f3 CORRECTLY NOT IMPLEMENTED: rejected amendment — TankSnapshot still exposes molt_stress_index and recent_events with detailed MoltFailure/MoltStressWarning events including cause codes and summaries","fr-7-63a03cd8 VERIFIED FIXED: summary probe uses distinct _summary wrapper functions with unique artifact labels via probe_artifact_label() helper at line 228; standalone tests and summary test no longer share artifact directories","fr-7-7ca6ed81 VERIFIED FIXED: light-depth probe at line 719-726 now requires growth_shallow > 0.0 (positive growth guard) in addition to the relative ordering check growth_shallow > growth_deep","All acceptance criteria satisfied: (1) molt success depends on GH/Ca/Mg/condition/reserve/instability/thermal, (2) 19+ molt parameters are named on ShrimpRuntimeParams with preset support and invariant validation, (3-4) unit tests cover GH monotonicity, Ca/Mg contribution, condition impact, failed molt mortality, stage-varied frequency, (5) 1000-hour soft-vs-hard integration passes with Ca/Mg-deficient source water, (6) emit_molt_failure covers 8 diagnostic cause codes with detail strings"],"findings_or_gaps":["fr-7-e444967f PARTIALLY ADDRESSED: The biofilter-scaling probe's build_state closure at e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:330-337 still seeds nitrifier biomass as carrying_capacity_g * INITIAL_CAPACITY_FRACTION, where carrying_capacity_g depends on media area. The larger-media run (4000 cm²) therefore starts with proportionally more nitrifier biomass than the smaller-media run (500 cm²), as shown in the test output: capacity small=0.747g vs large=1.278g. The assertion message at line 467 misleadingly says 'after the same seeded biomass warm-up' but the seeded biomass is NOT the same. While the assertions were improved from cumulative exposure to terminal reduced-N and biomass (which is less tautological), the fundamental starting advantage remains, weakening the probe's ability to discriminate between 'more media leads to more colonization/growth' vs 'more media starts with more bacteria and stays ahead'."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Fix biofilter probe seeding to use a fixed initial nitrifier biomass for both small and large media runs, e.g. seed both with the same absolute amount (the smaller carrying capacity * INITIAL_CAPACITY_FRACTION, or a fixed constant). This way the assertions on terminal reduced-N and final nitrifier biomass genuinely test whether more surface area promotes colonization and growth during the simulation, rather than preserving a head start."]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"978b1b1b-b3c0-4ff6-ae3e-ef315fdc3596"}
